From 918d668cd6f17dd0e33a24ac26f6b4063f4063e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 16:00:03 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] feat(cli): pr noun (ship/preflight/shepherd/merge) + gate doc
 (P2, 6ab3f30c)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Introduce the `pr` noun over the existing PR commands and fold doc-gate under
the existing `gate` noun, per the command-surface unification design (epic
eea186fa, phase 2). No handler logic moves — the noun surfaces route to the SAME
ship/preflight/shepherd/merge/doc-gate handlers.

- lib/commands/pr.js: thin noun dispatcher (mirrors the P1 memory noun); delegates
  ship/preflight/shepherd/merge at call time so the standalone commands stay the
  single source of truth for their own behaviour.
- lib/commands/gate.js: `gate doc [sub]` delegates to the doc-gate handler.
- lib/commands/_aliases.js: ship/preflight VISIBLE shortcuts, shepherd/merge/doc-gate
  HIDDEN back-compat aliases; canonical `pr `/`gate ` forms so they never enter the
  issue flag-passthrough set (shepherd/ship flags keep parsing intact).
- bin/forge.js: route the canonical noun form of a stage (`pr ship`) through the
  SAME top-level stage dispatch as the bare verb, so stage-entry enforcement +
  kernel stage-run recording + ensureForgeHome apply identically. Detected via the
  declarative alias map (subcommand is a stage AND its bare alias's canonical is
  exactly `<noun> <sub>`) — only `pr ship` matches today.

Backward-compat is byte-identical: bare ship/preflight/shepherd/merge/doc-gate
behave exactly as before (proven by CLI-spawn diff of stdout+stderr+exit code,
including `pr shepherd <pr> --pull --json` and `pr ship` stage enforcement).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
